From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:15:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtualization: leave the APEX payload to the product

The common APEX defaults pin an EROFS payload with 32 KiB physical
clusters. A product chooses its payload filesystem, compressor and
cluster size for every APEX through PRODUCT_DEFAULT_APEX_PAYLOAD_TYPE and
PRODUCT_DEFAULT_APEX_PAYLOAD_EROFS_*, and these two properties would
override all three for com.android.virt alone. Drop them so the APEX
follows the product like every other one.
---
 build/apex/Android.bp | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/apex/Android.bp b/build/apex/Android.bp
index f24eb80001f3e8f8cd730b27e2efc9a52be73269..c35c287c2c2772106f6654f42ead107183bad6f2 100644
--- a/build/apex/Android.bp
+++ b/build/apex/Android.bp
@@ -200,11 +200,6 @@ apex_defaults {
         true: "AndroidManifest.xml",
         default: unset,
     }),
-
-    payload_fs_type: "erofs",
-    erofs: {
-        pcluster_size: 32768,
-    },
 }
 
 apex_defaults {
